WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.750
The workbook's sixth chapter runs the
reconciliation over saved exports.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.837
On day one, the fictional estate shows
attribute drift, missing identities,

3
00:00:09.837 --> 00:00:13.775
orphan accounts, stale access,
and one unauthorized write.

4
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:18.713
Credential and schema drift are reported
as not computed, never as zero.

5
00:00:18.713 --> 00:00:22.043
On day two, HR corrects
a department to the value

6
00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:25.374
someone had already typed
into Entra ID by hand.

7
00:00:25.374 --> 00:00:26.863
The counts don't change.

8
00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:29.963
A comparison by finding
I D shows what moved.

9
00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:33.500
Entra now matches HR, so
that finding resolves.

10
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.388
SailPoint hasn't re-read
yet, so a new finding opens.

11
00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:39.533
The unauthorized write stays open,

12
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:43.526
because HR agreeing afterward
doesn't make the write authorized.

13
00:00:43.526 --> 00:00:47.352
The comparison refuses two runs
that computed different classes,

14
00:00:47.352 --> 00:00:50.413
since otherwise a skipped
class would look resolved.

15
00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:53.038
And a resolved finding is only a lead.

16
00:00:53.038 --> 00:00:55.440
Its record still closes on a re-read.
